# CQ 24: Which data have no stated origin?
#
# Clause 8.6.1 has data acquired from a source, and isAcquiredBy records that.
# Data without it appears in a model with no account of where it came from.
#
# For an audit this is the first question. A dataset a system was trained on
# and whose origin is unrecorded cannot be checked for the licence it came
# under, the consent it rests on, or the population it represents.
#
# Test case 3 answers with all four of its datasets, and that is a property of
# the case rather than of the pattern: it describes a hybrid architecture and
# leaves the data pipeline to the other two cases.
#
# The kinds are collected per dataset. A dataset may carry more than one, as
# production data that is also input data, and reporting each on its own row
# would say the same thing twice.
PREFIX iso:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?data (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?kindName; separator=", ") AS ?kinds)
WHERE {
  ?data a ?dataKind . ?dataKind rdfs:subClassOf* iso:Data .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?data a ?narrower .
                      ?narrower rdfs:subClassOf+ ?dataKind ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf* iso:Data }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?data iso:isAcquiredBy ?any }
  BIND(REPLACE(STR(?dataKind), ".*#", "") AS ?kindName)
} GROUP BY ?data ORDER BY ?data
